    topic: 'God Cares for His People – Protection',
    topicCode: 'SS2-CRS-04',
    module: "God's Providence",
    term: 'First Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Throughout Israel\'s journey from Egypt to Canaan, God repeatedly demonstrated His <span class="learn-keyword">protection</span> and <span class="learn-keyword">care</span> for His people in the wilderness. This topic examines specific examples of divine protection and what they mean for divine care today.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Protection at the Red Sea</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">When Pharaoh\'s army pursued the fleeing Israelites, God parted the Red Sea, allowing Israel to cross on dry ground while the pursuing Egyptian army was destroyed when the waters returned (Exodus 14:21-31). This event became Israel\'s defining memory of God\'s saving power.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Provision of Manna and Quail</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">In the wilderness, when Israel had no food, God provided manna — bread from heaven — every morning, and quail for meat, sustaining the entire nation for forty years (Exodus 16:4-15, 35).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Water from the Rock</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">When the people thirsted at Rephidim, God instructed Moses to strike the rock at Horeb, and water flowed out to satisfy the whole community (Exodus 17:1-7). A similar provision occurred later at Meribah (Numbers 20:8-11).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. The Pillar of Cloud and Fire</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">God guided and protected Israel continuously through a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night, which also stood between Israel and the Egyptian army at the Red Sea, protecting them from attack (Exodus 13:21-22; 14:19-20).</p>\n\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Form of Protection</th><th>Scripture</th><th>Need Met</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Parting of the Red Sea</td><td>Exodus 14</td><td>Escape from Pharaoh\'s army</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Manna and quail</td><td>Exodus 16</td><td>Daily food in the wilderness</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Water from the rock</td><td>Exodus 17; Numbers 20</td><td>Water in a dry land</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Pillar of cloud and fire</td><td>Exodus 13:21-22</td><td>Guidance and protection day and night</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish clearly between manna (bread-like food each morning) and quail (birds provided as meat), and know the two separate rock-striking incidents at Rephidim (Exodus 17) and Meribah (Numbers 20).\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> God\'s repeated provision and protection in the wilderness — deliverance from enemies, daily food, water, and guidance — reveal His faithful, continual care for His people, a truth Christians can still rely on today.\n</div>\n',
